<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Limits of this design</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Nothing checks availability.</strong> A voiceml.org document can&rsquo;t look anything up or remember earlier calls, so every booking is accepted, even for a full room. The restaurant&rsquo;s text is the only record. Checking tables needs a server.</li>
		<li><strong>Landlines don&rsquo;t get the text.</strong> The confirmation goes to the number the caller rang from; if it can&rsquo;t receive texts, that message fails and the call carries on.</li>
		<li><strong>The times are fixed in the document.</strong> Changing the menu of times means publishing again and pointing the number at the new URL.</li>
		<li><strong>Callers can&rsquo;t change a booking.</strong> The text asks them to call the restaurant instead.</li>
	</ul>
</section>

